# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Teerachote Pakornchote et al. (2023). StrainTensorNet: Predicting crystal structure elastic properties using SE(3)-equivariant graph neural networks.
#   Physical Review Research. doi:10.1103/physrevresearch.5.043198  arXiv:2306.12818v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2306.12818v2 (sha256 0f073cbf0302e4e1...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 74 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. StrainTensorNet is an
# SE(3)-equivariant graph neural network that predicts the strain energy
# density of strained crystal graphs and, from it, the elastic tensor and
# elastic moduli. It is a property-prediction model and not an
# interatomic potential: it predicts no atomic forces and defines no
# potential energy surface over atomic positions.

